{
  "kanda": "ayodhya",
  "sarga": 95,
  "title": "Rama and Seetha spend some time at Mandakini River",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/ayodhya/sarga95/ayodhyasans95.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/ayodhya/sarga95/ayodhyaitrans95.htm",
  "translator": "K. M. K. Murthy",
  "introduction": [
    "Rama describes to Seetha the beauty of Mandakini River with its multi-coloured beaches, swans, geese, deer and flowery trees on its banks. He shows some sages taking dip in the river and herds of elephants and monkeys coming for a drink there. Thus Rama and Seetha spend some of their time in enjoying the charms of Chitrakuta mountain."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इत्यार्षे श्रीमद्रामायणे आदिकाव्ये अयोध्याकांडे पंचनवतितमः सर्गः",
    "Thus completes 95th Chapter of Ayodhya Kanda of the glorious Ramayana of Valmiki, the work of a sage and the oldest epic."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "2.95.1",
      "label": "2.95.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "अथ शैलाद् विनिष्क्रम्य मैथिलीम् कोसल ईश्वरः |\nअदर्शयत् शुभ जलाम् रम्याम् मन्दाकिनीम् नदीम्",
